{"units": [{"id": "mvp-comment-58-1-mentioned12", "translation": "for the interruptions"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-58-1-mentioned13", "translation": "appropriate to the emotions"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-58-1-mentioned14", "translation": "b"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-58-1-mentioned15", "translation": "c"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-58-1-mentioned16", "translation": "a"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-58-1-mentioned17", "translation": "b"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-58-1-mentioned18", "translation": "c"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-58-1-mentioned19", "translation": "c"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-58-1-mentioned20", "translation": "a"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-58-1-mentioned21", "translation": "b"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-58-1-mentioned22", "translation": "b"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-58-1-mentioned23", "translation": "b"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-58-1-mentioned24", "translation": "c"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-58-1-mentioned25", "translation": "according to a bacchius"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-58-1-mentioned26", "translation": "c"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-58-1-mentioned27", "translation": "under the diaphragm"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-58-1-mentioned28", "translation": "under the lobe"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-58-1-mentioned29", "translation": "around the foot"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-58-1-mentioned30", "translation": "around the head"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-59-1-comment1", "translation": "The first wakes the second and has her wake the third, and meanwhile herself wakes a fourth who is addressed (⟦1⟧); for that this should mean \"as I you\" is hardly credible. The first ⟦2⟧ can be understood as \"awake\"; for this must precede the waking of another; so ⟦3⟧, namely ⟦4⟧ or ⟦5⟧, cf. ⟦6⟧ \"stop\". At ⟦7⟧ a change of speaker is possible; Paley compares Homer B 23 (cf. above p. 81) ⟦8⟧, ⟦9⟧; ⟦10⟧ (⟦11⟧) a strong word; from the singular there is a transition to the plural as in Ar. \"⟦12⟧. 203 (Weckl.) ⟦13⟧."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-59-1-mentioned1", "translation": "but I you"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-59-1-mentioned2", "translation": "awake"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-59-1-mentioned3", "translation": "yourself"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-59-1-mentioned4", "translation": "yourself (feminine)"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-59-1-mentioned5", "translation": "stop"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-59-1-mentioned6", "translation": "you are sleeping"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-59-1-mentioned7", "translation": "you are sleeping"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-59-1-mentioned8", "translation": "son of Atreus"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-59-1-mentioned9", "translation": "to kick away"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-59-1-mentioned10", "translation": "Birds"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-59-1-mentioned11", "translation": "having woken my nightingale we call them"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-59-2-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ is the dream, as ⟦2⟧ (⟦3⟧) is the death-cry and its cause;"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-59-2-mentioned1", "translation": "prelude"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-59-2-mentioned2", "translation": "they prelude"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-59-3-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ (⟦2⟧ or ⟦3⟧) also ⟦4⟧. ⟦5⟧."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-59-3-mentioned1", "translation": "to be vain"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-59-3-mentioned2", "translation": "to be vain"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-59-3-mentioned3", "translation": "to become"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-60-1-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧: as ⟦2⟧. ⟦3⟧;"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-60-1-mentioned1", "translation": "Alas, alas"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-60-2-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ cf. ⟦2⟧ ⟦3⟧ A, from which ⟦4⟧ Arist. '⟦5⟧. 680 is derived. Yet this is an exclamation of astonishment;"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-60-2-mentioned1", "translation": "pipax"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-60-2-mentioned2", "translation": "puppax"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-60-2-mentioned3", "translation": "to cry puppax"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-60-2-mentioned4", "translation": "Hipp."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-60-3-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ here rather ⟦2⟧, as ⟦3⟧ 146; accordingly ⟦4⟧ Aldina Ddf."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-60-3-mentioned1", "translation": "popax"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-60-3-mentioned2", "translation": "expressing indignation"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-60-3-mentioned3", "translation": "alas"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-60-3-mentioned4", "translation": "popax"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-60-4-comment1", "translation": "— The ⟦1⟧ is the escape of the fugitive, who is really gone; the ⟦2⟧, and indeed ⟦3⟧, are the many vain toils of the pursuit."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-60-4-mentioned1", "translation": "suffering"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-60-4-mentioned2", "translation": "to suffer much"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-60-4-mentioned3", "translation": "in vain"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-60-5-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ only here;"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-60-5-mentioned1", "translation": "ill-sounding"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-60-6-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ (⟦2⟧. 469, below 479, five times in Ag.) likewise only in A. and indeed in this trilogy (in prose ⟦3⟧). The hiatus after the interjection does not yet compel one to assume that the synaphea is interrupted before ⟦4⟧ and ⟦5⟧."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-60-6-mentioned1", "translation": "unbearable"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-60-6-mentioned2", "translation": "unbearable"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-60-6-mentioned3", "translation": "unbearable evil"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-60-6-mentioned4", "translation": "bitter to parents"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-61-1-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧: as ⟦2⟧ ⟦3⟧, got out; ⟦4⟧ Arist. ⟦5⟧. 970 (before ⟦6⟧). Then ⟦7⟧' (Abresch) instead of ⟦8⟧'; here the connection is too close for ⟦9⟧ to be tolerated."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-61-1-mentioned1", "translation": "he has fallen out of the nets"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-61-1-mentioned2", "translation": "he has fallen out of the evils"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-61-1-mentioned3", "translation": "Frogs"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-61-1-mentioned4", "translation": "if he falls into evils"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-61-1-mentioned5", "translation": "he is gone"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-61-1-mentioned6", "translation": "d'"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-61-1-mentioned7", "translation": "de"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-61-1-quote1", "translation": "having fallen out of the race"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-62-1-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧: agrees little with the strophe (◡ — ◡ — ◡ —) and has a striking syllaba anceps at the end of a first dochmius of the dimeter, as ⟦2⟧ ⟦3⟧ is emended) / ⟦4⟧. Here one must let the transmitted text stand; also in the strophes 778ff. and 837ff. similar things occur."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-62-1-mentioned1", "translation": "Alas, child of Zeus"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-62-1-mentioned2", "translation": "lead me out of the way"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-62-1-quote1", "translation": "lead me as quickly as possible"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-62-2-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ as Hom. (⟦2⟧ 364 etc.);"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-62-2-mentioned1", "translation": "deceitful"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-62-2-mentioned2", "translation": "l"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-62-3-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ middle as 199. ⟦2⟧ etc. (more often active)."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-62-3-mentioned1", "translation": "you may be"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-63-1-comment1", "translation": "- 150 very similar to 731 ⟦1⟧; also 778=808 ⟦2⟧, ⟦3⟧; the verb stands in its literal sense ⟦4⟧ ⟦5⟧ (devastated)."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-63-1-mentioned1", "translation": "since you ride me down, an old woman, young as you are"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-63-1-mentioned2", "translation": "younger gods"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-63-1-mentioned3", "translation": "you have ridden down the old laws"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-63-1-mentioned4", "translation": "the horse rode down the Megarian land"}]}